abstract:
Let $	heta_3(	au)=1+2\sum_{
u=1}^{\infty} q^{
u^2}$ with $q=e^{i\pi 	au}$ and $\Im (	au)>0$ denote the Thetanullwert of the Jacobi theta function \[	heta(z|	au) \,=\,\sum_{
u=-\infty}^{\infty} e^{\pi i
u^2	au + 2\pi i
u z} \,.\] Moreover, let $	heta_2(	au)=2\sum_{
u=0}^{\infty} q^{{(
u+1/2)}^2}$ and $	heta_4(	au)=1+2\sum_{
u=1}^{\infty} {(-1)}^{
u}q^{
u^2}$. For every even integer $n\geq 6$, which is not a power of two, we prove constructively the existence of a nontrivial integer polynomial $Q_n(X,Y)$ such that \[Q_n\Big( \, rac{	heta_3^4(n	au)}{	heta_3^4(	au)}, rac{	heta_2^4(	au)}{	heta_3^4(	au)}\, \Big) \,=\, 0 \] holds for all complex numbers $	au$ from the upper half plane of $\mathbb{C}$. These polynomials are used to prove the algebraic independence of $	heta_3(n	au)$ and $	heta_3(	au)$ for all algebraic numbers $q=e^{i\pi 	au}$ with $0<|q|<1$. Combining this with former results of the authors, it is shown that for such algebraic $q$ the numbers $	heta_3(n	au)$ and $	heta_3(	au)$ are algebraically independent over $\mathbb{Q}$ for every integer $n\geq 2$. A result on the algebraic dependence over $\mathbb{Q}$ of the three numbers $	heta_3(\ell	au)$, $	heta_3(m	au)$, and $	heta_3(n	au)$ for integers $\ell,m,n\geq 1$ is also presented.
